  "discussion": "Surf along north and west-facing shores near or at warning levels tonight are due to the current large, long- period north-northwest swell. The swell appears to have peaked at buoy 51001 midday, and the resultant surf is expected to peak overnight. Surf will be on the decline Wednesday, however a new extra large, long-period north-northwest swell is expected to arrive Wednesday night into Thursday that is expected to bring another round of warning level surf to north- and west- facing shores before gradually fading into the weekend. Surf heights along east-facing shores got a bump as the current north swell wraps into east shores. Another round of wrapping swell is possible with the extra large north-northwest swell on Thursday into Friday. This swell will shift more northerly with time, so more swell energy will make it into east-facing shores by Friday even as the swell begins fading.",
